<title>INDIA: India produces 46,384 tonnes aluminium in January.</title>
<headline>India produces 46,384 tonnes aluminium in January.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 46,384 tonnes of aluminium in January 1997 against 46,540 tonnes in December 1996, a government statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>The country produced 434,334 tonnes of aluminium between April 1996 and January 1997 compared with 429,739 tonnes in the same period a year earlier, the statement said.</p>
<p>It said the state-run National Aluminium Company Ltd exported 48,001 tonnes of alumina and 6,629 tonnes of aluminium in January, 1997.</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	    Installed   January, 1997     Cumulative output</p>
<p>	    capacity    --------------    ----------------</p>
<p>	    (annual)	 Output	 Apr96-Jan97 Apr95-Jan96</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> BALCO    100,000	  7,802	     76,459	76,921</p>
<p> INDAL    117,000	  3,575	     33,177	52,435</p>
<p> HINDALCO 210,000	 15,283	    135,779     143,788</p>
<p> NALCO    218,000	 17,815	    169,385     156,595</p>
<p> MALCO     25,000	  1,909	     19,534	   nil</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Total    670,000	 46,384	    434,334     429,739</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes.</p>
